---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="About This Trip" description="Why this retro Route 66 diary exists" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <article class="about-card">
        <h1>About This Trip</h1>

        <p>
          This is David’s Route 66 diary from Santa Monica to Albuquerque — part travel log, part
          questionable life decisions, all documented in glorious retro-road-software style.
        </p>

        <p>
          The vibe is intentionally early-2000s map program energy, but mobile-first so updates can
          be posted from airport gates, hotel lobbies, parking lots, and anywhere with enough
          signal to send a sentence.
        </p>

        <p>
          Every stop gets a dated entry with what actually happened: the plan, the detours, the
          food, and the occasional chaotic plot twist. If it’s in here, it happened (or at least
          felt true at the time).
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .about-card {
    border: 2px solid #8db4ff;
    background: #fff;
    padding: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
